{
  "_readme": "Rules per case. must_not: none of these substrings may appear (case-insensitive). must_all_groups: every group needs at least one of its substrings. soft=true turns a failed rule into WARN (fuzzy wording checks). status = expected HTTP status (default 200). user: A = adopter WITH applications (nandini), B = throwaway adopter with none, null = no token. Facts assume the demo data in CLAUDE.md: only Luna is AVAILABLE; Rex(1)/Milo(2)/ShelterLinkedPet/ShelterOnePet are ADOPTED, ShelterTwoPet is PENDING_ADOPTION. Cases run in order (memory cases depend on it). Restart the server first: chat memory is in-memory.",
  "global_must_not": [
    "Exception",
    "at com.petadoption",
    "Bad Gateway",
    "sk-",
    "Bearer eyJ",
    "jdbc:",
    "api.generative",
    "OPENAI_API_KEY",
    "Bearer sk-"
  ],
  "cases": [
